# Styling and Tailwind CSS Rules

## Tailwind CSS Standards
- Use Tailwind CSS for all styling
- Follow the design system defined in `@plane/propel`
- Use `clsx` and `tailwind-merge` for conditional classes
- Prefer utility classes over custom CSS

## Class Organization
```typescript
import { clsx } from "clsx";
import { twMerge } from "tailwind-merge";

const buttonClasses = clsx(
  "px-4 py-2 rounded-md font-medium",
  "bg-blue-500 text-white",
  "hover:bg-blue-600 focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500",
  "disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed",
  isActive && "bg-blue-700",
  twMerge(className) // Allow override classes
);
```

## Component Styling Patterns
- Use consistent spacing scale (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64)
- Follow the color palette from the design system
- Use semantic color names when possible
- Implement proper focus states for accessibility

## Responsive Design
```typescript
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
  {/* Responsive grid */}
</div>
```

## Dark Mode Support
- Use `next-themes` for theme management
- Implement dark mode variants using `dark:` prefix
- Test components in both light and dark modes

## Custom CSS
- Minimize custom CSS in favor of Tailwind utilities
- Use CSS modules only when necessary
- Place global styles in `styles/globals.css`
- Use CSS custom properties for dynamic values

## Design System Integration
- Import components from `@plane/ui` and `@plane/propel`
- Follow established component patterns
- Use consistent typography scale
- Implement proper loading and error states